special_abilities:
  - { choose: 1, from: ["Bushman Type: Classic", "Bushman Type: Explorer", "Bushman Type: Desert Nomad"] }
  - { name: "Bushman Type: Classic", description: "The standard Bushman and the majority of the class (printed 58). Psionics differ from the other two types: instead of 1D6 I.S.P. per level, the Classic Bushman gains a bonus of 2D6+6 I.S.P. at levels 2, 6 and 12, and at third level also gets Sixth Sense and one Sensitive or Physical power of choice. The sheet rolls the standard 1D6 per level and does not add the third-level powers; adjust by hand." }
  - { name: "Bushman Type: Explorer", description: "A born explorer who pushes into uncharted wilderness and trades what he has learned (printed 57). The second number of Memory for Details is +20%, so 50% +3% per level." }
  - { name: "Bushman Type: Desert Nomad", description: "Lives in the deserts rather than the bush (printed 57-58). Internal Compass is +10%, so 70% +3% per level. Blend applies to the desert instead of the bush, and the G.M. may apply -25% to survival rolls made in the bush. The only Bushman who may learn Hand to Hand: Assassin, at the cost of two other skill selections. Dresses in sand-colored hooded cotton robes with a face mask, lighter shoes and silt goggles, but carries the same gear." }
  - { name: "Iron Will", description: "Special ability 1 (printed 58). +1D4 M.E., +1 to save vs mind control and illusions, +3 to save vs disease, poison and pain, and +1 to save vs Horror Factor at levels 1, 3, 5, 6, 8, 10, 12 and 15. All of it is applied on the sheet." }
  - { name: "Internal Compass", description: "Special ability 2 (printed 58). Senses the correct direction by instinct and small telltale signs, can detect north, and rarely gets lost. Base skill 60% +3% per level (+10% for Desert Nomads)." }
  - { name: "Memory for Details", description: "Special ability 3 (printed 58). Terrain, wildlife, vegetation and fine detail of every new region are committed to memory. Base skill 60%/30% +3% per level; the second number is +20% for the Explorer. The first number is recalling and retelling stories, finds and directions accurately. The second is recognizing elements from past experience that give rudimentary information about an area: where a community has most likely settled and what kind of people they may be, likely predators and demons, common land formations and plants, and the location or likelihood of water." }
  - { name: "Instinctive, Minor Psionics", description: "Special ability 4 (printed 58). Every Bushman is a minor psionic with I.S.P. equal to M.E. plus 1D6 per level (the Classic Bushman instead gains 2D6+6 at levels 2, 6 and 12). Powers are limited to Summon Inner Strength, Resist Thirst, Empathy (with animals only) and the Super power Hypnotic Suggestion (natural, normal animals only). The Bushman regards these as old Bushman tricks, not psychic powers." }
